---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../config";
import { DIESEL_PRICES, DIESEL_UPDATED } from "../../data/cpm-data";

const updated = "August 22, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Trip Fuel Cost Calculator — Route A to B Diesel Cost (2026)"
  description="Calculate the real fuel cost of a truck trip between two US cities: real driving distance, your MPG, and the latest EIA diesel price for your region — before you accept the load."
  canonical={`${SITE.url}/calculators/trip-fuel-cost/`}
>
  <div class="calc-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Free Trucking Calculator</span>
      <h1>Trip Fuel Cost Calculator</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Know the <strong>fuel cost of the load before you accept it</strong>. Enter
        origin and destination, your MPG, and your region's diesel price — the real
        driving distance is computed automatically.
      </p>
      <div class="updated-badge" title="Diesel: EIA weekly survey 8/17/2026 · Routes: OSRM/OpenStreetMap">
        ⚡ Updated {updated} · diesel {DIESEL_UPDATED} · free forever
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container calc-body">
    <section class="calc-card">
      <h2>Trip details</h2>
      <div class="form-grid">
        <label>
          Origin (city, state)
          <input id="origin" type="text" placeholder="e.g. Dallas, TX" />
        </label>
        <label>
          Destination (city, state)
          <input id="dest" type="text" placeholder="e.g. Los Angeles, CA" />
        </label>
        <label>
          Average MPG
          <input id="mpg" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="1" step="0.1" value="6.2" />
        </label>
        <label>
          Diesel price region
          <select id="region">
            {DIESEL_PRICES.map((d) => (
              <option value={d.price} label={`${d.label} — $${d.price.toFixed(3)}`}></option>
            ))}
          </select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="form-grid" style="margin-top:.8rem;">
        <label style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;font-weight:600;">
          <input id="roundTrip" type="checkbox" /> Round trip (loaded + empty return)
        </label>
        <label>
          Safety buffer on miles (%)
          <input id="buffer" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" max="30" step="1" value="5" />
        </label>
      </div>
      <button id="calcBtn" class="btn-add">Calculate trip cost</button>
      <p id="err" class="zip-error" hidden></p>
    </section>

    <section class="calc-card" id="results" hidden>
      <h2>Your trip fuel cost</h2>
      <div class="result-summary">
        <div class="r-box">
          <span class="r-label">Driving distance</span>
          <span class="r-value" id="rMiles">—</span>
        </div>
        <div class="r-box">
          <span class="r-label">Fuel needed</span>
          <span class="r-value" id="rGallons">—</span>
        </div>
        <div class="r-box r-box-main">
          <span class="r-label">Fuel cost</span>
          <span class="r-value" id="rCost">—</span>
        </div>
        <div class="r-box">
          <span class="r-label">Cost / mile</span>
          <span class="r-value" id="rPerMile">—</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note" id="rNote"></p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- CONTENU ÉDITORIAL (SEO) -->
  <div class="container">
    <section class="editorial">
      <h2>Why trip fuel cost is the first number to check on any load</h2>
      <p>
        Before you accept a load, the fuel bill for the trip is the one cost you can
        predict almost exactly. Distance × your truck's MPG × the price of diesel where
        you fill up. This calculator does that math with a <strong>real driving
        distance</strong> (routed on OpenStreetMap data) instead of a straight-line
        guess, which can understate a route by 10-20%.
      </p>
      <p>
        The result is the minimum the load must pay, before maintenance, insurance,
        your time, or profit. Most owner-operators target fuel at roughly 40-45% of
        their gross revenue per load — if the fuel cost eats more than that, the load
        is probably not worth taking.
      </p>

      <h2>How to use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Enter origin and destination as city, state (e.g. "Dallas, TX").</li>
        <li>Set your real MPG — loaded, not the empty highway number. 6.2 is a fair class 8 average.</li>
        <li>Pick the diesel region closest to where you will actually fuel.</li>
        <li>Check "round trip" if you return empty — that doubles the fuel bill and is the classic hidden cost.</li>
        <li>The 5% safety buffer covers detours, re-routes, and idling at shippers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Example: Dallas, TX → Los Angeles, CA</h2>
      <p>
        The routed distance is roughly 1,430 miles one way. At 6.2 MPG with the
        national diesel average (${`$${DIESEL_PRICES[0].price.toFixed(3)}`}/gal), one way
        costs about <strong>${`$${((1430 / 6.2) * DIESEL_PRICES[0].price).toFixed(0)}`}</strong>.
        Round trip with an empty return: roughly double. Compare that against the load's
        rate before you commit — if the round-trip fuel alone is over a third of the
        pay, the math is tight.
      </p>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>How accurate is the driving distance?</summary>
          <p>
            The distance comes from OSRM routing on OpenStreetMap data — the same kind
            of routing used by truck apps. It follows real roads and gives highway
            distances that match what a truck would drive. It does not know truck
            restrictions (low bridges, weight limits), so add your safety buffer.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Should I include idling and traffic?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. The 5% default buffer covers detours and light delays. If you expect
            heavy congestion (Northeast corridors, Chicago), bump it to 8-10%. Idling
            for hours at a shipper or dock burns fuel without moving — add a flat amount
            if you know you will wait.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What MPG should I use?</summary>
          <p>
            Use your loaded average from your ELD or fuel records, not the truck's
            empty sticker number. A loaded class 8 typically does 5.5-7 MPG depending
            on terrain, speed, and weight. If you do not know, 6.2 is a safe default.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where do the diesel prices come from?</summary>
          <p>
            The EIA (U.S. Energy Information Administration) publishes a weekly on-highway
            diesel price survey by region. The dropdown uses the latest release
            ({DIESEL_UPDATED}) — the same numbers the industry press reports.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does this include tolls or IFTA?</summary>
          <p>
            No — this is fuel only. Tolls (turnpikes, bridges) are separate and can add
            $100-$400 on cross-country routes. IFTA taxes are inside the pump price.
            Use the IFTA calculator for quarterly fuel tax, and add tolls manually from
            the turnpike authority rate tables.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- METHODOLOGY -->
  <div class="container">
    <section class="method">
      <h2>Methodology &amp; sources</h2>
      <p>
        Distance: OSRM routing on OpenStreetMap data (router.project-osrm.org).
        Diesel prices: EIA Weekly On-Highway Diesel Survey ({DIESEL_UPDATED}).
        Cost = miles × (1 + buffer%) × roundTrip × diesel price ÷ MPG.
      </p>
      <p class="disclaimer">
        Planning tool for owner-operators and dispatchers. Actual routes, fuel stops,
        and prices vary. Always confirm load rates against your real numbers.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <style>
    .calc-hero { background: linear-gradient(120deg, #1c2a3a 0%, #2c4a63 70%, #3a6390 100%); color: #fff; padding: 2.2rem 0 2rem; border-radius: 14px; margin: 0 0 1.6rem; }
    .calc-hero .container { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.2rem; }
    .calc-hero .eyebrow { display: inline-block; background: rgba(255,255,255,.14); color: #ffd9a0; font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; padding: .3rem .7rem; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: .8rem; }
    .calc-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 4vw, 2.4rem); margin: 0 0 .6rem; line-height: 1.15; }
    .calc-hero .lead { font-size: 1.02rem; color: #e2ecf5; max-width: 680px; margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.55; }
    .updated-badge { display: inline-block; background: rgba(255,255,255,.12); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.25); color: #eaf4fb; font-size: .82rem; padding: .35rem .8rem; border-radius: 8px; }
    .calc-body { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.2rem; }
    .calc-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #dfe4ea; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.05); }
    .calc-card h2 { margin: 0 0 .9rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
    .form-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap: .9rem; }
    .form-grid label { font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 600; color: #333; }
    .form-grid input, .form-grid select { display: block; width: 100%; margin-top: .3rem; padding: .6rem .8rem; font-size: .95rem; border: 2px solid #c9d2dc; border-radius: 8px; font-family: inherit; background: #fff; }
    .form-grid input:focus, .form-grid select:focus { outline: none; border-color: #2c4a63; }
    .btn-add { background: #1c2a3a; color: #fff; border: none; font-weight: 700; padding: .7rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; font-size: .95rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
    .btn-add:hover { background: #2c4a63; }
    .btn-add:disabled { opacity: .6; cursor: wait; }
    .zip-error { color: #b3261e; font-size: .9rem; margin: .7rem 0 0; }
    .result-summary { display: flex; gap: .8rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .r-box { flex: 1 1 160px; background: #f3f7fb; border: 1px solid #d8e3ee; border-radius: 10px; padding: .9rem 1rem; text-align: center; }
    .r-box-main { background: #1c2a3a; border-color: #1c2a3a; }
    .r-label { display: block; font-size: .75rem; color: #4a6a85; font-weight: 600; }
    .r-box-main .r-label { color: #a8c4dd; }
    .r-value { display: block; font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #1c2a3a; margin: .25rem 0; }
    .r-box-main .r-value { color: #ffb85c; }
    .note { color: #55544e; font-size: .85rem; margin: .8rem 0 0; line-height: 1.5; }
    .editorial { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto 2rem; padding: 0 1.2rem; }
    .editorial h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 2rem 0 .7rem; }
    .editorial p, .editorial li { font-size: .95rem; color: #3d3d38; line-height: 1.65; }
    .editorial ul { padding-left: 1.3rem; }
    .faq details { border: 1px solid #dfe4ea; border-radius: 10px; padding: .8rem 1rem; margin-bottom: .6rem; background: #fff; }
    .faq summary { font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; color: #1c2a3a; font-size: .95rem; }
    .faq details p { margin: .6rem 0 0; font-size: .9rem; color: #55544e; line-height: 1.6; }
    .method { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto 2rem; padding: 0 1.2rem; }
    .method p { font-size: .92rem; color: #3d3d38; line-height: 1.6; }
    .disclaimer { font-size: .82rem; color: #7a7870; font-style: italic; }
  </style>

  <script>
    import { geocode, routeMiles, computeTrip } from "../../lib/trip";
    const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!;

    $("calcBtn").addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const origin = $("origin").value.trim();
      const dest = $("dest").value.trim();
      $("err").hidden = true;
      if (!origin || !dest) { $("err").textContent = "Enter both origin and destination."; $("err").hidden = false; return; }
      const btn = $("calcBtn");
      btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = "Routing…";
      try {
        const a = await geocode(origin);
        const b = await geocode(dest);
        const miles = await routeMiles(a, b);
        const i = {
          miles,
          mpg: parseFloat($("mpg").value) || 6.2,
          dieselPrice: parseFloat($("region").value) || 5.454,
          roundTrip: ($("roundTrip") as HTMLInputElement).checked,
          safetyBufferPct: parseFloat($("buffer").value) || 5,
        };
        const r = computeTrip(i);
        $("rMiles").textContent = `${Math.round(r.totalMiles).toLocaleString()} mi`;
        $("rGallons").textContent = `${r.fuelGallons.toFixed(0)} gal`;
        $("rCost").textContent = `$${r.fuelCost.toFixed(0)}`;
        $("rPerMile").textContent = `$${r.perMile.toFixed(2)}`;
        $("rNote").textContent = `${a.name} → ${b.name} · ${i.roundTrip ? "round trip" : "one way"} · ${i.mpg} MPG · ${i.safetyBufferPct}% buffer · diesel ${`$${i.dieselPrice.toFixed(3)}`}/gal`;
        $("results").hidden = false;
      } catch (e) {
        $("err").textContent = "Could not route that trip. Check the city names (e.g. \"Dallas, TX\").";
        $("err").hidden = false;
      } finally {
        btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = "Calculate trip cost";
      }
    });
  </script>

  <!-- JSON-LD FAQPage -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How accurate is the driving distance?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The distance comes from OSRM routing on OpenStreetMap data — real roads, highway distances that match what a truck would drive. It does not know truck restrictions, so add your safety buffer." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Should I include idling and traffic?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. The 5% default buffer covers detours and light delays. Bump it to 8-10% for congested corridors, and add a flat amount if you know you will wait at a dock." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "What MPG should I use?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Use your loaded average from your ELD or fuel records. A loaded class 8 typically does 5.5-7 MPG. If you do not know, 6.2 is a safe default." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Where do the diesel prices come from?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The EIA publishes a weekly on-highway diesel price survey by region. The dropdown uses the latest release." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Does this include tolls or IFTA?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No — this is fuel only. Tolls are separate and can add $100-$400 on cross-country routes. IFTA taxes are inside the pump price." } }
    ]
  })} />
</BaseLayout>
